 "_about": "The repository owner's answers to Tools/data/filter_candidates.json, given on the review page on 2026-09-27: for each item, each suggested tag and whether to add it. Tools/build/apply_filter_tags.py applies them.",
 "_revised": "2026-09-27, by the owner: q1644/q1648 (Tome of Divinity -- 10 Linen Cloth, which humanoids drop) and q6123/q6128 (Gathering the Cure -- Earthroot, and Lunar Fungus or Kodo Horns, all gathered or dropped) can be done without the Auction House; q61's tagged step is the trip to Stormwind for Shipment to Stormwind, not part of Hogger. Later the same day: the Auction House tag belongs on the step that sends you there, not on a quest you can also do another way. The fishing quests (q1141, q5386, q5421) are no longer tagged; Look To The Stars (q174: Bronze Tubes drop, and a vendor sometimes has one) keeps the tag on its buy steps only; notes that are about farming (q136, q185, q605, q3785, q3786, the Silk Cloth notes) are no longer tagged. Quests that need a crafted item -- q1073, q4244, q40190, q40730, q40735, q40736 -- keep theirs. 2026-09-28, at the owner's request: three reviewed steps had another quest's id. Jammal'an the Prophet (Alliance, Hinterlands) was filed as q3528, The God Hakkar: it is q1446, whose ST answer it shares. Seeing What Happens and Return to Ironforge were filed as q2963, Portents of Uldum: they are q2946 and q2977, and keep its ULDA answer. Yuka Screwspigot was filed as q2768, Divino-matic Rod, whose Zul'Farrak tag it took: it is q4324, and its quests are in Blackrock Depths, so the owner's dungeon answer is BRD.",
 "_followups": "Quests you can only pick up after a quest tagged whole, with the tag they inherit and the quest they follow -- derived from pfQuest's prerequisites by Tools/build/apply_filter_tags.py --pfquest, not answered by anyone.",
